	Talking of stupid deaths ......

	Lot of hackers have written about stupid deaths of low level 
characters. What about stupid deaths of high level characters?

	I had a Level 30 Wizard, lots of intrinsics, +8 Excalibur, 
+11 Frostbrand, max. luck, all kinds of goodies, -43 AC, around 180 HP.
Teleported down to level 50. Cleaned up the level. No problem. Found a
crystal ball. Now, the problem with Hell, is they are levels of no return,
except level teleporting ofcourse. Because I was carrying a lot of stuff,
I could not carry the crystal ball up to the previous level. I wanted it, 
so I could locate stuff easily (like gemstones). So to reduce weight, what
do I do ?????

	Eat a K-ration.

	"You choke over your food. You die -more-"
	Do you want to see your intrinsics?

	What I could not understand was why the program did not ask me
if I was satiated? I was under the impression that  if you were satiated
the program would ask you if you wanted to continue eating. In this case
it did not do so !! Is this a feature of the game ?? This has happened to 
me several times.

General Comments about that game:

1) IMHO the wizard is one of the most powerful characters.

2) A blessed luckstone can do wonders for your game. I found a magic lamp
and wished for gray dragon scale mail. Recharged and wished for the luckstone.

3) In case some of you are wondering about the +11 Frostbrand - I DID NOT
know it was +11 until after the game was over. I had got it after sacrificing
at an altar. This was after I had the luckstone and max. luck. I enchanted it
twice with blessed scrolls of enchant weapon. So I actually got a blessed
+5 Frostbrand from my deity !! I naturally assumed it would be +0 enchantment.
I don't think I would enchanted the second time if I knew it was +8 !!


	But all is not lost. The game left a bones level. I can't wait to 
get to that level !!


